' Source: apps/api-node/src/modules/posts/application/post.use-cases.ts
' Main entity migration: apps/api-node/src/migrations/002_lost_found_schema.sql
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Guest / User" as Actor
participant "Posts Page" as Page
participant "Posts API" as API
participant "Post Service" as Service
participant "posts" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Search and filter posts
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: GET /api/posts?search=...&type=...&page=...
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate optional session and filters
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Search and filter posts
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Normalize search; validate category, location, order and page
Service -> Table: 6: SELECT visible board posts using supported filters
activate Table
Table --> Service: 7: Filtered posts and total
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 8: Apply viewer-specific privacy serialization
Service --> API: 9: Filtered board with correct page total
API --> Page: 10: HTTP 200: Filtered board with correct page total
Page --> Actor: 11: Show authorized result
deactivate Service
else Invalid input or request unavailable
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Related tables, authorization, transactions and audit remain inside the service. Catalogue status is
not deployment or manual acceptance.
endlegend
@enduml
